  "foaf:name": "Deepsea Microbial Omics for Environment and Health",
  "sdo:name": "Deepsea Microbial Omics for Environment and Health",
  "sdo:description": "OMICS-DEEP investigates deep-sea microbial ecosystems in Pacific and Indian Ocean seafloors (4000-11000m depth) using metagenomics, metaproteomics, and culturomics. This initiative addresses knowledge gaps in how extreme deep-sea microbes function, adapt, and impact human health. The program will examine health risks from deep-sea microorganisms, evaluate impacts of deep-sea mining/pollution on microbial communities affecting human health, and explore therapeutic potential for human society. Through comprehensive microbial multi-omics analysis, OMICS-DEEP will develop standardized protocols, analysis platforms, and predictive models linking deep-sea microbial processes to human health. Emphasizing capacity building, international collaboration, and open data sharing, OMICS-DEEP contributes to sustainable deep-sea management, health protection, biotechnological innovation, and scientific foundation for policy decisions on deep-sea conservation under anthropogenic pressures.",
  "sdo:location": "China",
  "sdo:identifier": "72.9",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/deepsea-microbial-omics-for-environment-and-health/",
